-- Three section GIVENs whose symbols a naive scheme could merge: two named
-- `x` in different sections (the second gets a numbering suffix) and one
-- whose own name is `x#2`. Each must keep its own symbol.
§ `Inner`
    GIVEN x IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A NUMBER
`inner x` MEANS x

§ `Outer`
    GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
          `x#2` IS A NUMBER

-- refuted: three independent numbers
#ASSERT x PLUS `inner x` EQUALS `x#2`
